# API key scopes and scheduled jobs (added in 1.0.3)
ApiKeyScopesHelp = Minimum key scopes: PHONE_NUMBERS_READ, CONVERSATIONS_READ, SMS_SEND, CRM_READ. See the
DocApiScopes = API key scopes
DocApiScopesText = When creating the key in Allo (Settings > API), only tick the scopes of the features you use:
DocScopeFeature = Module feature
DocScopeTestNumbers = Connection test and number list
DocScopeCalls = Call log synchronization
DocScopeSMS = SMS sending
DocScopeContacts = Contact synchronization (read only, the module does not write to Allo)
DocApiScopesNote = Webhooks are configured in the Allo interface and need no scope. A missing scope returns HTTP 403 API_KEY_INSUFFICIENT_SCOPE with the name of the required scope.
DocCron = Scheduled jobs
DocCronText = Alternative to the webhook when Dolibarr cannot be reached from the internet: Dolibarr polls Allo at regular intervals. Two jobs are created when the module is enabled, disabled by default:
DocCronCalls = every hour, imports and updates the call log of every configured number
DocCronContacts = once a day, synchronizes Allo contacts (only if "Enable contact sync" is ticked in the setup)
DocCronEnable = To enable them: activate the Scheduled jobs module, then Home > Admin tools > Scheduled jobs. The Dolibarr system cron (scripts/cron/cron_run_jobs.php) must be set up.
DocTroubleshootScope = "API_KEY_INSUFFICIENT_SCOPE" error
DocTroubleshootScopeFix = The API key lacks the scope required by the feature (see the API key scopes section). Create a new key in Allo with that scope and save it in the setup.
AlloCallsSyncJob = Allo - Call sync
AlloContactsSyncJob = Allo - Contact sync
